		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-02-10T06:42:39Z",
			"File": [
				"⡿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				59,
				11
			],
			"Message": "feat(Grove): Implement host function execution and stabilize API surface\n\nCompletes the Wasmtime 20 integration by activating the host function bridge and refining the public API for the `Grove` extension host.\n\n**WASM Runtime & Function Export:**\n- Replaced the `FunctionExport` placeholder with a concrete implementation using `linker.func_wrap` compatible with Wasmtime 20.\n- Implemented synchronous host function wrapping that handles `i32` input/output marshaling, JSON serialization/deserialization, and error-to-trap mapping.\n- Added detailed performance logging for executed host functions and improved error propagation.\n\n**Transport & Module Structure:**\n- Refactored `TransportStrategy` implementations (gRPC, IPC, WASM) to import types from the flattened `Transport` module rather than internal paths, resolving visibility issues introduced by the `Impl` suffix migration.\n- Updated `mod.rs` to re-export `TransportType` and `TransportStats` for public consumption.\n\n**Tooling & CLI:**\n- Updated `main.rs` to utilize the new `RuntimeBuild::build_host_with_defaults` API and the explicit extension ID-based activation flow.\n- Added JSON logging support to `Cargo.toml` for structured telemetry.\n- Relaxed documentation enforcement to a warning and added `allow` directives for non-standard casing to accommodate FFI and generated bindings.\n\n**Spine Protocol:**\n- Enhanced documentation in `SpineActionClient` to clarify the current stub status of the EchoAction listener and heartbeat loop pending the final bidirectional streaming implementation.\n\n**Impact:** The `Grove` host can now successfully execute Rust functions invoked from WASM guests, closing a critical gap in the extension host's capabilities.",
			"SHA": "46218c83cc1faccacb91e0cb121bc44c6e4b1ea3"
		}
	],
